ptember show a dead heat, with several Republican-sponsored surveys and one nonpartisan KSTP/SurveyUSA poll tied. Flanagan has raised more money and drawn millions in outside support, while Tafoya has leaned on welfare-fraud attacks. The forecast lands on a modest but real Democratic edge, wider than the polls alone suggest but short of safe.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8725, "margin": 5.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7776, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8131, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8217, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7867, "margin": 5.0}]}